%p.mb-3
  Download the
  = link_to('form_complete.js file', '/javascripts/widgets/form_complete.js', rel: 'nofollow', class: 'fw-bold')
  and put it on your server.

%p.mb-3
  Add this script to your HTML page's
  %code= '<head>'
  section:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code
    = preserve do
      :escaped
        <script src="form_complete.js" type="text/javascript" charset="utf-8"></script>

%p.mb-3
  This example assumes
  %code form_complete.js
  is in the same folder as your HTML page. If you save it elsewhere, update the script's
  %code src
  path.

%p.mb-3
  Add this input to your form to search #{@ontology.acronym}. Selecting a class places its full URI in the field:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code
    = preserve do
      :escaped
        <input type="text" name="term" class="bp_form_complete-#{CGI.escape(@ontology.acronym).gsub('-', '%2D')}-uri">

%p.mb-3
  The widget searches the latest version of the ontology. Give each autocomplete input a unique
  %code name
  so its associated hidden fields can be identified.

%h6.mt-4 Choose the field value
%p.mb-3
  The input's
  %code class
  attribute uses this format:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code bp_form_complete-{ontology_id_list}-{value}
%p.mb-3
  Replace the final
  %code uri
  in the example with the value you want to display after a class is selected:
%table.table.table-sm
  %thead
    %tr
      %th{scope: 'col'} Value
      %th{scope: 'col'} Field content
  %tbody
    %tr
      %td
        %code uri
      %td The class's full URI
    %tr
      %td
        %code shortid
      %td The class's short ID
    %tr
      %td
        %code name
      %td The class's preferred name

%h6.mt-4 Search multiple ontologies
%p.mb-3
  Replace the input's widget class with a comma-separated list of ontology IDs:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code bp_form_complete-NCIT,NCBITAXON-uri
%p.mb-3
  Or search all ontologies in #{$SITE}:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code bp_form_complete-all-uri
%p.mb-3
  If an ontology ID contains a hyphen, replace that hyphen with
  %code %2D
  in the widget class. For example, use
  %code FB%2DDV
  for FB-DV.

%h6.mt-4 Access the selected class details
%p.mb-3
  The widget automatically creates four hidden inputs and fills them when a class is selected.
  Their IDs start with your input's
  = succeed '.' do
    %code name
  For the
  %code name="term"
  example above, it creates:
%pre.bg-light.border.rounded.p-3
  %code
    = preserve do
      :escaped
        <input type="hidden" id="term_bioportal_preferred_name">
        <input type="hidden" id="term_bioportal_concept_id">
        <input type="hidden" id="term_bioportal_ontology_id">
        <input type="hidden" id="term_bioportal_full_id">
%p.mb-3
  You can read these values with JavaScript. You do not need to add the hidden inputs yourself.

%p.mb-3
  See the NCBO Wiki for
  = succeed '.' do
    = link_to('additional configuration options', 'https://www.bioontology.org/wiki/NCBO_Widgets#Optional_attributes', target: '_blank')
%p.mb-0
  For more help visit the
  = succeed '.' do
    = link_to('NCBO Wiki', 'https://www.bioontology.org/wiki/NCBO_Widgets#Term-selection_field_on_a_form', target: '_blank')
